        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Quote Twice",
          "text": "The path is a SQL string in single quotes; string literals inside it take ==double== quotes: `'$.st ? (@ == \"open\")'`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Filters And Methods",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "'$.items[*] ? (@.qty > 10)'",
            "'$.name ? (@ like_regex \"^a\" flag \"i\")'",
            "'$.sku ? (@ starts with \"A-\")'",
            "'$ ? (exists(@.addr) && !((@.x > 0) is unknown))'"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`?()` is the filter, `@` is the current item",
            "Predicates: `== != < <= > >=`, `&&`, `||`, `!`, `exists()`, `is unknown`",
            "Methods: `.type() .size() .double() .abs() .floor() .ceiling()`",
            "Also `.keyvalue()` and `.datetime(template)`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Lax vs Strict",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "lax (default)",
                "lines": [
                  "Auto-unwraps arrays",
                  "Missing key = no match",
                  "Structural errors swallowed"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "strict",
                "lines": [
                  "Refuses to unwrap",
                  "Raises errors instead",
                  "Prefix path with `strict`"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Operators And Functions",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Form",
            "Takes"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`data @? '$.items[*] ? (@.qty>10)'`",
              "a locator"
            ],
            [
              "`data @@ '$.qty > 10'`",
              "a predicate"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Mixing up `@?` and `@@` is the classic beginner error",
            "`@?` asks: does the path return **any** item?",
            "`@@` wants a path that is itself a boolean"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Function Forms",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
