  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 3 of POSTGRES JSONB. Most Postgres jsonb bugs are not bugs — they are two operators that look identical and behave nothing alike. `data->>'k' = 'v'` cannot touch a GIN index; `data @> '{\"k\":\"v\"}'` can. Ten pages on storage, containment, jsonpath, GIN opclasses, TOAST, and the exact moment a key stops belonging in the document.",
